  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe Doosan DNM post always writes a bare `G84`. On a control where the rigid-tap parameter is not set, a bare `G84` is floating tapping, not rigid tapping. `fanuc.cps` has the option \"Rigid tap M29 before G84\". The Doosan post does not.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe Doosan DNM post has a `rigidTapM29` option. It is off by default and works as in `fanuc.cps`.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:1290-1310`: `onCycle` writes `G84` with no `M29`.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:65` and the `M29` block near `:1269`: the option in the Fanuc post.\n- FANUC Series 0i-F operator's manual B-64604EN-2/01, p. 90 (rigid tapping).\n- Related: #3498 (the open questions for M29 on a real control).\n\nFound by the post audit against the Fanuc manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\n- With the option on, the post writes `M29 S<rpm>` before each G84 group. A test pins it.\n- With the option off, the output does not change.\n",
